  "body": "## Accepted scope\n\nThis reconstructed theoretical edition proves the determinant-divisibility assertion in [Teufl\u2013Wagner Problem 1](https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/46745), printed pp. 1457\u20131458, for every n \u2265 1: (det A)^C_n divides det T in Z[a_ij], for generic A and the full Bell-partition forest transfer matrix. It fixes one unweighted tree per input block and counts each admissible interlayer edge subset once. There is no planarity, noncrossing-state, symmetry, positivity or numerical nonzero-row-sum restriction.\n\nThe conclusion is a divisor, not exact multiplicity of det A or irreducibility of the remaining factor. The full proof constructs the constant Catalan-dimensional quotient, determines its transfer determinant exactly, lifts through the invariant kernel, and uses Gauss's lemma for integer-polynomial divisibility.\n\n## Evidence and review\n\nThe complete 25,072-byte reconstructed proof and 14,983-byte fresh independent audit are included byte-for-byte. The audit accepts the exact present proof hash after checking all seven lemmas, normalization and signs, invariant spanning, ordered Gaussian factors, the constant kernel and integral descent. A separate full reading of the proof and audit also found no required mathematical change.\n\nThis is a newly checked reconstructed edition of the same first approach, not byte-for-byte recovery certified by an old checksum and not a new substantive research turn. The full written audit retains its supplementary finite-check discussion; no checker code, standalone fixtures, execution-result files or logs are included. The all-n conclusion rests on the written argument.\n\nThe forest algebra and Catalan/noncrossing quotient are established work of [Caracciolo\u2013Sokal\u2013Sportiello](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0706.1509v2) and [Sportiello\u2019s thesis, Chapter 10](https://pcteserver.mi.infn.it/~caraccio/PhD/Sportiello.pdf). Attribution, the bounded related-work review, five freshly retrieved public PDF identities and inspection history are retained. No novelty, historical-priority or current-open-status claim is made. The reviews are AI mathematical/source audits, not human peer review or formal proof-assistant verification.\n\n## Exact addition-only scope\n\nAdd exactly ten files under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30003822/`: the full proof, full fresh audit, attribution, acceptance, status and provenance, source catalogue/inspection metadata, README and noncircular manifest. No QUEUE.md or unrelated file changes.\n\nNo copied third-party source PDFs, text, HTML or images, dataset contents, private sources, derived source-text fingerprints, private inventories or private coordination material are included. File hashes and additive patch replay validate packaging integrity only.\n\n## File identity pins\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.md`: 2,999 bytes; SHA-256 `763e98a43aa03b66f3f6cf49cb207caf68e96e51e1a4d622b8eca713e82de9db`\n- `ATTRIBUTION.md`: 5,749 bytes; SHA-256 `63be59e02b08da4d9a9e8fe94b583a36857ed04aeb18160a7e28ec3626c81ae7`\n- `AUDIT.md`: 14,983 bytes; SHA-256 `2d2a03db98576bd58e9726198b3fd050f77cde68a97ef2b5670c6c538678285b`\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,925 bytes; SHA-256 `46d4e342f54f6744621a706ea1fd791ae6b53bae1d8fffe6c417a166b5f1cc94`\n- `PROOF.md`: 25,072 bytes; SHA-256 `546d9df387da3266b1b20d31b1cd6017a65fe9f497f1b37d2a99319e6194755c`\n- `PROVENANCE.md`: 4,930 bytes; SHA-256 `6ba54796dfe1295b56b2580b829d5fa0c72811721845f319ecfaf72182261c7e`\n- `README.md`: 3,194 bytes; SHA-256 `66fc6bb0febc3c48abe8eed680ca68727cf4212f6ad0d6c975c1c5bdbb5b110b`\n- `SOURCE_CATALOGUE.json`: 10,852 bytes; SHA-256 `85f9b233c22357681bde7b1807aeab71e9c09331a9ed741c1119d0065b4b815b`\n- `SOURCE_PROVENANCE.json`: 6,921 bytes; SHA-256 `8366cca42b727b72b2990620105afd5d13c1a07ee3798920633ca26033521348`\n- `STATUS.json`: 1,967 bytes; SHA-256 `a75a164e84a859bcd97cd500dd92359068c4dd150c8c2012886fa795dc086e0c`\n\nThe manifest lists all ten files and hashes the other nine; this body independently pins the manifest.\n",
